        "original_id": "acc22f34-d880-50c2-9ea6-c865ae3559b2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert H. Purcell, Stephen Feinstone, Albert Kapikian\n- Topics: Hepatitis A virus (HAV), Hepatitis A symptoms\n\nFacts:\n- Robert H. Purcell was born on 19 December 1935.\n- Robert H. Purcell is a virologist.\n- In 1973, Robert H. Purcell, Stephen Feinstone, and Albert Kapikian co-identified the Hepatitis A virus (HAV).\n- When Hepatitis A symptoms occur, they typically last eight weeks.\n- Hepatitis A symptoms may include nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, jaundice, fever, and abdominal pain.",
